What is an Anti-fog Lens?
An anti‑fog lens incorporates either a permanent material property (physical anti‑fog) or a surface treatment (chemical anti‑fog) that prevents the formation of microscopic water droplets on the optic surface. The technology typically relies on hydrophilic or hydrophobic nanostructured coatings that either spread moisture into a transparent film or repel water to maintain visual clarity. When combined with secondary functions such as anti‑scratch, UV blocking, or blue‑light filtering, the lens becomes a multi‑functional safety component.
